  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "The night before, mix the flour, yeast, water, sugar, salt and soft butter in a mixer with a dough hook for 8 minutes until the dough is pliable and not sticky. Cover and refrigerate overnight."
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast the eggplant until soft and scoop out 100 g of flesh. Mix it with the cheeses, egg yolk, salt and pepper in a bowl."
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 180°C."
    },
    {
      "text": "Roll the dough out to 3-4 mm thick and cut 10 cm rounds. Place a teaspoon of filling in the centre of each, fold into half-moons and press the edges with a fork. Brush with beaten egg and sprinkle with sesame seeds. Place on a tray with space between them."
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for about 20 minutes until golden. If freezing, wait until the pastries cool to room temperature."
    }
  ],
